def logged(function):
    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):
        return function(*args, **kwargs)
    return wrapper

@logged
def area(width, height):
    """Return the area."""
    return width * height

print(area.__name__, area.__doc__)
```

questions.explanation:
@logged replaces area with the wrapper function, so its name and docstring are the
wrapper's. Decorating wrapper with @functools.wraps(function) copies the name,
docstring and other attributes from the original.

