@dataclass
class Point:
    x: int
    y: int

seen = {Point(1, 2)}
```

questions.explanation:
@dataclass generates __eq__ by default, and a class that defines __eq__ without
__hash__ is unhashable. @dataclass(frozen=True) makes instances read-only and
generates a __hash__ from the fields, so they can go in sets and be dict keys.

